  "solution": "**Given: **\n\nfrac{{{{sin }²}{{63}^°} + {{sin }²}{{27}^°}}}{{{{cos }²}{{17}^°} + {{cos }²}{{73}^°}}}\n\n**Concept used:**\n\nsinθ = cos (90 - θ)\n\ncosθ = sin (90 - θ)\n\ncos²θ + sin²θ = 1\n\n**Calculations:**\n\n⇒ frac{{{{sin }²}{{63}^°} + {{sin }²}{{27}^°}}}{{{{cos }²}{{17}^°} + {{cos }²}{{73}^°}}} \n\n⇒ frac{{{{sin }²}{({90}^°- {27}^°)} + {{sin }²}{{27}^°}}}{{{{cos }²}{{17}^°} + {{cos }²}{({90}^°-{17}^°})}}\n\n⇒ frac{{{{cos }²}{{27}^°} + {{sin }²}{{27}^°}}}{{{{cos }²}{{17}^°} + {{sin }²}{{17}^°}}}\n\n⇒ {1 over 1}\n\n⇒ 1\n\n**Hence, the value of the given expression is 1.**\n\n35:Tb7c,\n<p&g",
